# What a transpiler of classes writes. If the clock of the order of start took the call of the function for "whatever it enters may run from here on", nothing that the body lays would be laid at any known time:
# each method of Parser stayed behind a guard. One call enters that body, once, where the start passes once: it is part of the start.
# SINCE 11-04 (R257) THE CLOCK OF START SAYS OF NO NAME THAT IT IS LAID AHEAD: through a hole in it the read of such a name gave undefined where the type said a function, and the process died; the claim fired on no program that we are judged by. What this test told apart by `laid-ahead` it no longer tells.
# RUN: link members layouts mechanisms=all
# CHECK: on-prototype L0 "peek" function=f{{*}}
# CHECK: layout L0 {{*}}prototype-object-settled
# The function is called twice . an object is made ahead of the call.
# RUN(NOT): link members mechanisms=all
# NOT-NOT: "m" {{*}}laid-ahead

